Here is a simple Python script that uses Flask as a web framework to achieve a screensharing app. This script will create a URL for the user to share and then return a link to be shared with others.

Please note that this script is very basic and doesn't include any kind of authentication, authorization, or error handling. You may want to add these features depending on your needs.

```Python
from flask import Flask, request, jsonify
import uuid
import time

app = Flask(__name__)

# This dictionary will store the URLs and their corresponding IDs
urls = {}

# This function generates a unique ID for each URL
def generate_id():
    return str(uuid.uuid4())

@app.route('/share', methods=['GET'])
def share():
    url = request.args.get('url')
    if url:
        id = generate_id()
        urls[id] = url
        return jsonify({'link': f'https://example.com/mirror/{id}'})
    else:
        return jsonify({'error': 'URL is required'}), 400

@app.route('/mirror/<id>', methods=['GET'])
def mirror(id):
    if id in urls:
        url = urls[id]
        return jsonify({'url': url})
    else:
        return jsonify({'error': 'Invalid ID'}), 404

if __name__ == '__main__':
    app.run(debug=True)
```

